{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Realtime Pattern Validator",
  "description": "Validate Socket.IO and real-time messaging patterns",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "flutter_chat_app/lib/core/network/**/*socket*.dart",
      "flutter_chat_app/lib/core/services/**/*realtime*.dart",
      "src/modules/chat/**/*gateway*.ts"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Validate real-time implementation:\n\n**FLUTTER SOCKET MANAGER PATTERN:**\n```dart\n@singleton\nclass EnhancedSocketManager {\n  final Socket _socket;\n  final StreamController<SocketEvent> _eventController;\n  \n  // Connection management\n  Future<void> connect() async {\n    if (_socket.connected) return;\n    \n    _socket.connect();\n    \n    // Setup listeners\n    _socket.on('connect', _onConnect);\n    _socket.on('disconnect', _onDisconnect);\n    _socket.on('error', _onError);\n    \n    // Reconnection logic\n    _socket.on('reconnect_attempt', _onReconnectAttempt);\n  }\n  \n  // Event emission with acknowledgment\n  Future<void> emit(String event, dynamic data) async {\n    if (!_socket.connected) {\n      throw SocketException('Not connected');\n    }\n    \n    _socket.emitWithAck(event, data, ack: (response) {\n      // Handle acknowledgment\n    });\n  }\n  \n  // Stream-based event listening\n  Stream<T> on<T>(String event) {\n    return _eventController.stream\n        .where((e) => e.name == event)\n        .map((e) => e.data as T);\n  }\n  \n  // Cleanup\n  Future<void> dispose() async {\n    await _eventController.close();\n    _socket.dispose();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**NESTJS GATEWAY PATTERN:**\n```typescript\n@WebSocketGateway({\n  cors: { origin: '*' },\n  namespace: '/chat',\n})\nexport class ChatGateway implements OnGatewayConnection, OnGatewayDisconnect {\n  @WebSocketServer()\n  server: Server;\n  \n  constructor(\n    private readonly chatService: ChatService,\n    private readonly logger: LoggerService,\n  ) {}\n  \n  async handleConnection(client: Socket) {\n    this.logger.log(`Client connected: ${client.id}`);\n    \n    // Authenticate\n    const user = await this.authenticateSocket(client);\n    if (!user) {\n      client.disconnect();\n      return;\n    }\n    \n    // Join user's rooms\n    await this.joinUserRooms(client, user);\n  }\n  \n  async handleDisconnect(client: Socket) {\n    this.logger.log(`Client disconnected: ${client.id}`);\n    // Cleanup\n  }\n  \n  @SubscribeMessage('sendMessage')\n  async handleMessage(\n    @ConnectedSocket() client: Socket,\n    @MessageBody() data: SendMessageDto,\n  ): Promise<WsResponse<Message>> {\n    // Validate\n    // Process\n    const message = await this.chatService.createMessage(data);\n    \n    // Broadcast to room\n    this.server.to(data.chatId).emit('newMessage', message);\n    \n    // Acknowledge\n    return { event: 'messageSent', data: message };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**CHECK FOR:**\n\n**Flutter:**\n✅ Singleton socket manager\n✅ Connection state management\n✅ Reconnection logic\n✅ Event acknowledgments\n✅ Stream-based event handling\n✅ Proper disposal\n✅ Error handling\n✅ Rate limiting\n\n❌ Multiple socket instances\n❌ No reconnection logic\n❌ Memory leaks (not disposing)\n❌ No error handling\n❌ Blocking operations\n\n**NestJS:**\n✅ @WebSocketGateway decorator\n✅ Authentication in handleConnection\n✅ Room management\n✅ @SubscribeMessage handlers\n✅ Broadcasting to rooms\n✅ Acknowledgments\n✅ Error handling\n✅ Logging\n\n❌ No authentication\n❌ No room management\n❌ Synchronous handlers\n❌ No error handling\n❌ Broadcasting to all (use rooms)\n\n**PERFORMANCE:**\n- Use rooms for targeted broadcasting\n- Implement rate limiting\n- Batch events when possible\n- Use binary data for large payloads\n- Implement heartbeat/ping-pong\n\nReport violations and suggest proper real-time patterns."
  }
}
